        "description": "Instead of fixing centers first, jointly optimize all 78 variables (52 center coordinates + 26 radii) in a single optimization call. Formulate as maximizing sum(radii) subject to constraints: (1) r_i + r_j <= dist(i,j) for all pairs, (2) r_i <= min(x_i, y_i, 1-x_i, 1-y_i) for boundaries. Use scipy.optimize.minimize with SLSQP method which handles nonlinear constraints. Start from the current hexagonal solution as warm start. Run multiple random restarts with different initial perturbations to escape local optima. The key insight is that centers and radii should co-evolve, not be sequential.",
